00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:58.020
blocks. And chords are sort of like learning&nbsp;
how to build simple structures. For example:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:04.620
this apple tree, or this watermelon. So&nbsp;
learning chords is kind of like learning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:13.800
how to build these simple Lego structures which&nbsp;
you can then later use to build even more complex&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:20.220
bigger Lego structures. And once you have this&nbsp;
skill of seeing music from the lens of chords,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:26.220
music doesn't become so scary anymore, because&nbsp;
all you see are these sort of simple structures&nbsp;&nbsp;

